        {
          "id": 2709557583,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "My reasoning is that since the \"standard\" Bluetooth HCI Command dissector is still being used (top level \"Bluetooth HCI Command - Vendor Command 0xfc1c\") it would make sense to keep this section full - all fields should be defined (e.g. \"Parameter Total Length\" is duplicated, so if Parameter should be omitted why keep the length?).\n\nAlternatively, if the vendor dissector is found, the standard one should not be used, e.i.: show only the \"Bluetooth Broadcom HCI\". However, in such case standard filtering might not work, because \"Bluetooth HCI Command\" uses different keys than \"Bluetooth Broadcom HCI\" - `bthci_cmd.param_length` vs `bthci_vendor.broadcom.parameter_length`.\n\nThe final decision is on your side of course, I'm just trying to show my point of view, because to be honest, I'm not sure which way will be better :D",
          "author": {
            "id": 4497865,
            "username": "arkq",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Arkadiusz Bokowy",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/4497865/avatar.png?v=1777447120",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/arkq"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-26T13:00:12.086Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-26T15:21:54.814Z",
          "system": false,
